{"author":"tfm2mods · flover","dependencies":[{"mod_id":"base","version":">=0.6.4, <0.6.5"}],"last_updated":"2026-10-14","mod_id":"tfm2_champ_pos_lock","name":"TFM2 Champion Position Lock: Rework","version":"1.0.1","description":"TFM2 Champion Position Lock: Rework\n\nOriginal mod: Champion Position Lock by tfm2mods.\nRework: flover.\n\nThis rework keeps the original position-lock concept while changing the safety/fallback rules and making the UI easier to understand.\n\nMain behavior\n* Assign champions to Top / Jungle / Mid / Bot / Support in Settings -> Gameplay -> Position Lock.\n* Assigned champions are used first for their allowed positions.\n* The required count is NOT a fixed number. It is calculated from the current draft rules (series length, ban cards, Fearless / Hard Fearless, etc.).\n* A position does not need to reach the displayed safety requirement before its restriction starts working. If assigned champions exist, they are used first.\n* Only positions that actually share champions are checked together with the shared-pool/subset safety calculation. Unrelated short positions do not inflate each other.\n* Champions assigned to another position do not automatically become free picks.\n* Champions assigned to no position are the free-reserve pool. They stay locked while the designated pools can still fill the lineup.\n* If a designated position pool is actually exhausted by bans, picks or Fearless locks, that position alone may use free-reserve champions.\n* If no legal candidate exists even after reserve fallback, the final global fail-open remains as an emergency anti-deadlock safeguard.\n* The same rules are used by direct player drafting, AI drafting, head-coach delegation, AI position assignment and auto-swap.\n\nUI\n* Separates Selected / Base Requirement / Shared Pool so the reason for shortage is easier to understand.\n* Shows direct overlap counts per position (the same champion may appear in more than one overlap count).\n* Shows shared-pool checks only when relevant, including pass/fail details.\n* Shows whether user pick gate, AI/head-coach pick gate, AI assignment and auto-swap are enabled.\n\nCompatibility\n* Game: Teamfight Manager 2 v0.6.4.\n* Windows only.\n* Rework uses the SAME mod ID as the original Champion Position Lock (tfm2_champ_pos_lock), so only one of them can be installed. Install it by replacing the original's folder (mods\tfm2_champ_pos_lock).\n* Per-save position lists saved by the original are read as-is (same save format), and switching back keeps them too."}